<title>SWEDEN: Swedish govt sees unemployment above goal in 2000.</title>
<headline>Swedish govt sees unemployment above goal in 2000.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swedish government said on Tuesday it expected unemployment to fall to 4.5 percent in 2000, admitting it will not meet its pledge to halve unemployment to four percent by the turn of the century.</p>
<p>In its spring budget proposal it forecast unemployment would fall to 7.9 percent in 1997 and 7.1 percent in 1998, from March levels of 8.4 percent.</p>
</text>
